        "original_id": "7b335272-471d-5b11-b83a-966f42a35b28",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kristian Zahrtmann, Peder Severin Krøyer, Theodor Esbern Philipsen\n- Organizations: Skagen Painters\n- Places: Skagen, Denmark\n- Concepts: Danish artistic generation, Academicism, Golden Age of Danish Painting, naturalism, realism\n\nFacts:\n- Kristian Zahrtmann was born on 31 March 1843 and died on 22 June 1917.\n- Kristian Zahrtmann was a Danish painter.\n- Kristian Zahrtmann was part of the late 19th-century Danish artistic generation alongside Peder Severin Krøyer and Theodor Esbern Philipsen.\n- This Danish artistic generation broke away from traditional Academicism and the heritage of the Golden Age of Danish Painting in favor of naturalism and realism.\n- Peder Severin Krøyer was one of the best known, most beloved, and most colorful members of the Skagen Painters.\n- The Skagen Painters were a community of Danish and Nordic artists who lived, gathered, or worked in Skagen, Denmark, especially during the final decades of the 19th century.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
